{
  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_002: multimodal, singleprofile, scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l, concat fusion, acc≈0.532), the most fundamental uncertainty is whether multimodal fusion actually adds value over a unimodal baseline. config_005 (image_only, singleprofile, imagenet_vit_l, no aggregation) is the cleanest single-variable comparison to config_002—it removes only the RNA modality while keeping the same image encoder and profile setting. If image-only performs comparably (~0.53), it suggests the RNA signal contributes little and future effort should focus on image representation and aggregation; if it performs substantially worse, it confirms multimodal fusion is worthwhile and justifies further exploration of RNA encoders and fusion strategies. Establishing this unimodal baseline is more informative than testing a second fusion strategy or a different RNA encoder, because it resolves the highest-level design question (is multimodal necessary?) before committing budget to finer-grained comparisons within the multimodal space."
}

